The \(^{15}\mathrm{N}\) NMR spectrum of e-2–Mg2(dobpdc)– \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) (Figure 3c) exhibits resonances assignable to carbamate \((76~\mathrm{ppm})\) and ammonium \((42~\mathrm{ppm})\) groups, further supporting the formation of ammonium carbamate chains via reaction of the primary amine with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) . The secondary ammonium resonance is shifted by \(^{+8}\) ppm relative to the secondary amine resonance present in the activated material e-2–Mg2(dobpdc)—similar to previous \(^{15}\mathrm{N}\) NMR studies of ammonium carbamates.40–42 Overall, our multinuclear NMR experiments confirm that ammonium carbamate chain formation dominates for e-2–Mg2(dobpdc) and e-2– \(\mathrm{Zn}_{2}(\mathrm{dobpdc})\) (Figure S4).
